    },
    "body": "In `MainActivity.LogIn`, AES-GCM IV material now comes directly from `SecureRandom` instead of a string generator backed by `Random`. RVSec reported that the `GCMParameterSpec` call's IV material was not observed to come from a randomized source; the previous path did not directly provide randomized IV bytes.\n\nI removed the string generator, store the generated 12-byte IV as tagged hexadecimal, and decode it in `StartActivity` before decryption. The decoder retains the legacy untagged `getBytes()` behavior for existing stored values. Data written by this version is not readable by earlier versions of the app.\n\nI found this while running the app under RVSec, a runtime checker for how apps use the Java crypto and TLS APIs.\n\nThe project builds with this change (`assembleDebug`).\n\nI'm a Computer Engineering student at the University of Brasília (UnB), working on a research project on Android app analysis. Happy to adjust this to the project's conventions.",
